0..76 Comment "//! A pair written in a field of another pair whose type a definition\'s call"
77..90 Comment "//! computes."
91..94 Comment "//!"
95..170 Comment "//! The lowering reads the type of a constructor written in a field off the"
171..247 Comment "//! arguments of the type of the constructor around it. A call that computes"
248..326 Comment "//! that type gives the lowering no arguments to read. So the inner pair needs"
327..369 Comment "//! a type that the source does not state."
370..373 Comment "//!"
374..448 Comment "//! The lowering refuses the declaration by name at the inner pair, and it"
449..527 Comment "//! never drops it. An inner pair with its pair type written beside it checks."
528..571 Comment "//! One pair at a computed type checks too."
572..575 Comment "//!"
576..592 Comment "//! - see: #5373"
